  "pre_registration": {
    "question": "Does a frozen, quantitative single-copy sensitivity prediction (the exposed-trial BA contrast of one added exact copy, measured in R7-C6 / R6-C3a) anticipate the benchmark-level distortion of pairwise model gaps, the rank-crossing dose and model-selection regret when a controlled fraction of scored test trials has exact copies in training?",
    "evidence_status": "Lee2019 participants, folds, training / validation sets and the single-copy contrasts are those of R6-C3 / R7-C6 (54 known participants; not an independent cohort). No R11-B arm (CLEAN, PLACEBO, LEAKED at any dose, L40c) was ever fitted. The near-clean gaps are effectively known in advance (G0); the prospective endpoints are the dose arms. Not an external replication; not independent of the prediction source.",
    "dose": "delta = fraction of the 100 scored held-out-run trials whose exact copies are in training: 0.2, 0.4, 0.6, 1.0 (10, 20, 30, 50 per class; nested, class-stratified, outcome-blind). Fixed rows: every non-CLEAN arm holds 240 base + 100 extra rows (50 per class); L_delta's extra rows are 100 delta scored-trial copies plus 100 (1 - delta) base copies; PLACEBO's are 100 base copies (the delta = 0 point).",
    "primary_pair": "ShallowConvNet - EEGNet (identical tasks, base, pairs and recipe as R7-C6). Read-outs: final epoch and minimum-validation-loss epoch from the same runs. TS+LR pairs are secondary (their single-copy prior was measured on a 300-row base).",
    "H1_primary": "Distortion prediction D_pred(delta) = delta * dc (frozen). Loss = sum over 4 doses of squared participant error. Test L(competitor) - L(prediction) > 0 against ZERO (D = 0) and CEILING (every exposed trial correct for both models, from the observed PLACEBO arm), for final and ES: Holm over 4 (all discriminating a priori by the 2-point rule). Accuracy: 90 % CI of the cohort-mean error inside +/- 2 BA at every dose.",
    "H1_secondary": "The same for EEGNet - TS+LR and ShallowConvNet - TS+LR at both read-outs; only comparisons discriminating a priori (|prediction - competitor| >= 2 at some dose) count; Holm over those.",
    "classification": "per pair and read-out: CONTRADICTED if a discriminating competitor is significantly better; SUPPORTED_STRONG if the prediction beats every discriminating competitor (Holm) and is within +/- 2 BA at every dose; SUPPORTED_RELATIVE if it beats every discriminating competitor only; PARTIAL if some; else NOT_SUPPORTED.",
    "H2_crossing": "For pairs with a frozen eligible crossing prediction (prior gap CI below 0, dc > 0, bootstrap interval of delta* inside (0, 1]): primary ShallowConvNet - EEGNet (ES), delta* = 0.442 [0.297, 0.644]; secondary ShallowConvNet - TS+LR (final), 0.301 [0.109, 0.442]. delta*_obs = first zero crossing of the cohort-mean leaked-arm gap over (P, 0.2, 0.4, 0.6, 1.0), linear between points. Classes: CROSSING_AS_PREDICTED (inside the frozen interval), CROSSING_EARLIER / LATER_THAN_PREDICTED, NO_CROSSING_BY_1.0, NOT_EVALUABLE_PREMISE (the gap under PLACEBO is not negative).",
    "reversal": "At each dose, the R10-A rule on P -> L_delta with D tested per dose (Holm over the 4 doses of the pair and read-out): NO_REVERSAL / DESCRIPTIVE_REVERSAL / SUPPORTED_CROSSING / SUPPORTED_REVERSAL.",
    "selection": "Roster {TS+LR, EEGNet, ShallowConvNet} per read-out: choose by the LEAKED cohort mean at each dose; evaluate on the matched PLACEBO arm (primary) and on CLEAN. Regret relevant if >= 2 BA. A top-1 change counts as supported only if its pair is SUPPORTED_REVERSAL at that dose. Within-benchmark counterfactual only.",
    "decomposition": "delta = 0.4 split halves (H1 = S_0.4, H2 disjoint, class-stratified): E = OWN - OTHER (exposure at fixed support of 40 same-run copies) vs the single-copy c; S = OTHER - P (support). Stitched counterfactuals, descriptive.",
    "overall": "On R1: CONTRADICTED if the primary pair is CONTRADICTED at either read-out; SUPPORTED if it is SUPPORTED_STRONG at both read-outs and the ES crossing is CROSSING_AS_PREDICTED; PARTIAL if it is SUPPORTED_STRONG / RELATIVE at either read-out or the crossing is as predicted; else NOT_SUPPORTED. The final verdict is the lower of R1 and R2 (deep models re-trained with independent initialisation / order / dropout seeds; TS+LR is deterministic), order SUPPORTED > PARTIAL > NOT_SUPPORTED > CONTRADICTED.",
    "inference": "54 participants; t95; two-sided MC sign-flip 1e6 (seed 11399); participant bootstrap 20,000 (seed 11010); Holm within families; SESOI 2 BA points (vendored R4 / Paper A).",
    "forbidden_after_any_fit": "changing a dose, arm, seed, read-out, model, prediction, competitor, threshold, family or participant set; adding a model."
  },
